1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Referring to other online Goltz researchers who are quoting as their source the book "Nachrichten über die Familie der Grafen und Freiherren von der Goltz - Friedrich Freiherr von der Goltz - Strassburg 1885, Verla
2 CONC g R. Schultz und Comp.", it appears that this Kazimierz is not listed as an official son of Christian Heinrich Günther von der Goltz and Sophie Elisabeth von Oesterling;  according to the above german source it appears that the pa
2 CONC rents married in 1749, 5 years after Kazimierz was born. However, as of June 2017, I was able to find and obtain the baptism record from the church in Trzcianka where Kazimierz was baptized. The baptism record confirms that "Casim
2 CONC ir" was the son of "Henrici Golcz et Zofia Osterling" (in church latin), and further denotes that Henrici and Zofia were "legitimor. conjugum," or legitimately married, that Casimir was the son of a legitimate union. The baptism r
2 CONC ecord for March 1744, at the catholic church of Trzcianka, reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Łomnica, D 25, Idem baptisavi Casimirum die 18 Marty natum filium Generor Henrici Golcz et Zofia Osterling legitimor. conjugum. Patroni fuerant Christian B..dku (hard to read the last name, possibly Bedku, or Berdku, Budku, or sim
2 CONC ilar) et Anna Osten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Loosely translated this baptism record reads:  Łomnica, day 25 (of March). We herewith baptize Casimir, born 18 March, son of the family (race) of Henric Golcz and Zofia Osterling, legitimately married. Godparents (baptismal patro
2 CONC ns) were Christian B... and Anna Osten.
2 CONT
2 CONT This baptism record is squeezed in at the bottom of the page of other baptism records for that month, with what appears to be a different handwriting (messier) than the previous records. It also uses shorter form and is less verbo
2 CONC se than the baptism records that precede it. Possibly because it was being squeezed in at the bottom of the page.
2 CONT
2 CONT The mystery remains why Henryk and Zofia gave birth to Kazimierz in Łomnica, Trczianka, when, according to the german records, they later seem to have lived on their estate in Lubno (Lüben) near Walcz (Deutsch-Krone), and died at 
2 CONC their estate in Brotzen (Broczyno, southeast of Czaplinek), respectively 40 and 55 kilometers north of Łomnica.  And why is there is no mention in the german "Nachrichten..." book of this first son Casimir / Kazimierz?  
2 CONT
2 CONT One can speculate... Sophia, born in 1729, would have been only 14 at conception, Heinrich, born in 1725, 18. They would have been 15 and 19 at the birth, with Heinrich probably still in military school, possibly not yet married..
2 CONC . though the baptism record indicates otherwise.  Anyhow, while this remains a mystery, it seems to be confirmed by the baptism record that Casimir / Kasimierz is indeed the son of Henryk Golcz and Zofia-Elzbieta Osterling (as sta
2 CONC ted in Herbarz Polski published by Adam Boniecki.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Scan of the baptism record from Trzcianka catholic church, 25 March 1744.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Boniecki, Herbarz polski - 6.435.115 - t. VI s. 180: Golczowie v. Goltzowie v. Gulczowie h. Własnego
2 CONT
2 CONT Elżbieta Sęczys, Szlachta wylegitymowana - le.989.2.4 - Golcz h. Gulcz 
