1 TITL Heir Apparent Lüben and Appelwerder
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heinrich Golcz was Starost of Derpt, Lord and heir of Lubno (Lüben) and Appelwerder. In German nobility books he is called Christian Heinrich Günther 653 von der Goltz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There was another Heinrich Golcz, about 30 years older than him, who was Starost (district magistrate) for Walcz, and he's often mistaken for this Heinrich. Apparently they were second cousins and shared the same great grandparent
2 CONC s, Conrad (KONE) Reimer 604 von der Goltz, and Ida (Idea) 237 von Dewitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT The two Henryk cousins interacted at times, as evidenced in the Teki Dworzaczka court records of Walcz. The records differentiated between them as "Henryk of Lubno" and "Henryk Starost [of Walcz]."  For example, in 1756, he sold L
2 CONC ubno to Henryk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For more information, see:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Boniecki, Herbarz polski - 6.435.112 - t. VI s. 180: Golczowie v. Goltzowie v. Gulczowie h. Własnego
2 CONT
2 CONT sw.34502 Teki Dworzaczka, Regesty, WALCZ 3000 (1757 r.)  // Wałcz - 3102
