1 OCCU Представниця українського шляхетського роду Гостських, гербу Кирдій, відома меценатка, фундаторка, прихильниця право
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT notę by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT = Raina / Regina Hojska (Hoscka) Solomerecka
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess (knyaginya), a member of the Hojski (Hoscki) noble family. In the foundation charter of 1644 she is identified as “Raina Hoscka Solomerecka, wife of the Smolensk Castellan” (kasztelanowa smoleńska). In the registers of of
2 CONC ficials her name appears in the Polish form Regina Hoscka. The surname occurs in several variants in historical sources: Hoscka, Hostska, Hojska (East Slavic: Goskaya, Gostskaya, Goyskaya).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the wife of Prince Mikołaj Lew Sołomerecki, Pinsk Chamberlain (podkomorzy piński) and Castellan of Smolensk. In the register of Smolensk castellans he is listed as Mikołaj Lew Sołomerecki, husband of Regina Hoscka, Castell
2 CONC an of Kyiv’s daughter (kasztelanka kijowska). He died in late 1626 or early 1627.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raina belonged to a prominent family of Kyiv officials. Her father, Hawryło Hojski (Hoscki), first served as Standard-Bearer of Kyiv (chorąży kijowski) and was later appointed Castellan of Kyiv (kasztelan kijowski). In Urzędnicy W
2 CONC ielkiego Księstwa Litewskiego, vol. 3, fasc. 4, he appears under no. 3 as Hawryło Hojski. The register records him in office in 1605 and again in 1621, after which he is listed as Castellan of Kyiv. In the register of Kyiv castell
2 CONC ans he appears under no. 94 as Hawryło Hojski, formerly Standard-Bearer of Kyiv.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raina’s brother was Roman Hojski (Hoscki). In the register of Kyiv castellans he appears under no. 95 as Roman Hojski, Starosta of Volodymyr and son of the preceding office-holder, namely Hawryło Hojski. He is recorded as Starosta
2 CONC  of Volodymyr in 1625 and is associated with the Kyiv castellany from 1632 onward. Thus, Raina was the daughter of the Castellan of Kyiv and the sister of another prominent member of the same family who likewise held the office of
2 CONC  Castellan of Kyiv.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surviving sources preserve a foundation charter dated 1644. In this document Raina appears as the widow of Prince Sołomerecki and as a benefactress of the Orthodox Church. The charter records her donation to the Church of the 
2 CONC Dormition of the Mother of God in the town of Wysock, Pinsk District, granting the church a hay meadow known as “Mikolska Hrada”. The document emphasizes that the donation was made for spiritual benefit and perpetual commemoration
2 CONC , while expressly forbidding anyone from obstructing the clergy or the church in the possession and use of the donated property.
